///
/// TODO: replace `todo!()` with the three stats.
fn array_stats(prices: &[i32; 4]) -> (usize, i32, i32) {
    todo!()
}

// --- check (do not modify) ---
assert_eq!(array_stats(&[5, 2, 8, 1]), (4, 1, 16));
assert_eq!(array_stats(&[-1, -2, -3, -4]), (4, -4, -10));
assert_eq!(array_stats(&[7, 7, 7, 7]), (4, 7, 28));
println!("Exercise 1.1 passed");
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### Exercise 1.2 — Queries, not panics

**Goal**: answer three questions with `Option`/`bool` accessors instead of indexing.

**Info**: `first()`, `last()` and `is_empty()` never panic; indexing does. Absence is data here, so return it, do not crash on it.

**Objectives**

- return `(is_empty, longer_than_three, first_element)` as a tuple
- `first_element` is `None` when the slice is empty
- keep the signature unchanged

**See**: §1.2 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: `.first().copied()` converts `Option<&T>` into `Option<T>` for `Copy` types.
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="rust">
