///
/// TODO: replace `todo!()` with the measure-and-return.
fn growth_plan(inserts: usize) -> usize {
    todo!()
}

// --- check (do not modify) ---
assert_eq!(growth_plan(0), 0);
assert_eq!(growth_plan(1), 4);
assert_eq!(growth_plan(4), 4);
assert_eq!(growth_plan(5), 8);
println!("Exercise 2.1 passed");
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### Exercise 2.2 — Reserve once

**Goal**: fill a vector with zero reallocations by reserving first.

**Info**: `with_capacity(n)` allocates `n` slots up front; pushes underneath that bound never move the buffer.

**Objectives**

- return a `Vec<i32>` containing `0..n` (exclusive), built with a single allocation
- keep the signature unchanged

**See**: §2.2 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: `Vec::with_capacity(n)` then push, or `(0..n).collect()` — both are one allocation.
</VSCode.Cell>
