### Exercise 8.2 — Rotate and peek

**Goal**: preview a rotation without touching the original.

**Info**: `rotate_left(n)` walks every element toward the front by `n`, wrapping. It needs `&mut`, so a preview means a cheap clone of the deque (three words plus the buffer — elements are `Copy` here). One edge: `rotate_left` asserts `n <= len`, so an **empty** deque must be answered before any rotation.

**Objectives**

- return what the front element **would be** after `steps` rotations, as `Option`
- an empty deque returns `None` under any `steps`
- keep the signature unchanged; `q` itself must not change

**See**: §8.2 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: guard `is_empty()` first — an empty deque has no front under any rotation; `steps % probe.len()` keeps the rotation amount in range.
</VSCode.Cell>
<VSCode.Cell language="rust">
