## 16. Review: Mixed Problems

Two capstone exercises for this chapter: each one chains several sections at once.

### Exercise 16.1 — Distinct word lengths

**Goal**: from free text to a sorted set of word lengths in one pipeline.

**Info**: `split_whitespace` borrows the words; `len()` projects; `collect` into a `BTreeSet` deduplicates and sorts. String chapter, iterator chapter and set chapter in one chain.

**Objectives**

- return the set of distinct word **byte** lengths in `text`
- keep the signature unchanged

**See**: §9.3, §10.4 and §4.1 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: `text.split_whitespace().map(|w| w.len()).collect()` — the return type names the container.
