### Exercise 16.2 — Leaderboard: borrowed in, owned out

**Goal**: rank rows by score and return the top names as owned strings.

**Info**: sort the rows by score **descending** (a stable sort keeps equal scores in arrival order), take `n`, and project to owned `String`s — the borrowed-in/owned-out signature this chapter kept recommending.

**Objectives**

- return the names of the top `n` rows by score, best first
- ties keep arrival order
- keep the signature unchanged

**See**: §10.2 and §11.1 of the example notebook.

**Hint**: `rows.sort_by(|x, y| y.1.cmp(&x.1));` — comparing the score fields in reverse — then `take(n)` and `map` to `name.to_string()`.
</VSCode.Cell>
