<VSCode.Cell language="markdown">
### What Comes Next

Chapter 07 puts these containers to work on the outside world: files read into `String`s and `Vec`s, arguments arrive as a map-shaped iterator, and every fallible operation hands back a `Result` — the error side of the containers you just drilled.

- `07_io-and-files` — stdin/stdout/stderr, `std::fs`, buffered readers and writers
- `08_assertions-and-type-checks` — checking the assumptions your container code makes, at runtime and compile time
- `10_structs-oop-and-traits` — your own types inside these containers, and the traits that make them work

**Carry forward.** Solved, every exercise here is a reflex: `entry` for upserts, `get` over `[]` when absence is data, `&[T]` in signatures, `iter`/`iter_mut`/`into_iter` chosen on purpose, `with_capacity` when the size is known. If any check still fails, the matching section of the example notebook is the fastest fix.
</VSCode.Cell>
